SUMMARY:History of Tommy Thompson Park (Leslie Street Spit) (RETURN FOR 20
 26)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass
  is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, emai
 l**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for sign
 ing up!**\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount whe
 n booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following em
 ail at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nWelcome to Toronto History
  Walks!\n\nThis walk is the full history and story behind the building of 
 the Leslie Street Spit. From a popular beach in the 1950s to a nature sanc
 tuary this walk explores the human and natural history of the Park!\n\nOne
  of the best places to walk and enjoy the sights of Toronto is Tommy Thomp
 son Park. But it's not just a great place to see the sweeping views of Tor
 onto harbour\, but it's also a fascinating story of landfill operations an
 d has an historic undertone that dates back to the early twentieth century
 .\n\nOut of nothing comes something\, really should be the slogan for the 
 Leslie Street Spit.\n\nThis walk is not only a history walk\, it has some 
 of the best opportunities for picture taking\, and nature. So I hope to se
 e you there\, and bring your camera.\n\nOur walk begins at the southeast i
 ntersection of **Leslie St at Commissioners Street!** We return to the sta
 rt location after our adventure!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfe
 r the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-trans
 fer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
