SUMMARY:Hurricane Hazel 2026 (SPECIAL ANNIVERSARY EDITION)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nOn October 15\
 , 1954\, Toronto was devastated by the deadliest Hurricane of the 1954 sea
 son. Hazel was the most intense hurricane to hit the continent of North Am
 erica in 1954.\n\nPrior to the disaster that struck Toronto\, the storm ki
 lled 469 people in Haiti\, and the Caribbean before striking the United St
 ates. It roared ashore as a Category 4 hurricane.\n\nAfter causing 95 deat
 hs in the US\, Hazel struck Ontario\, raising the death toll by 81\, mostl
 y in Toronto. As a result of the high death toll and the damage caused\, i
 ts name was retired from use.\n\nBut Toronto gained so much from the 1954 
 disaster\, and our ravines and parklands are our lungs of the city. Thanks
  to Hazel we have our green spaces for generations to come.\n\nThis walkin
 g tour is for all levels and walkers with a few small hills and some steps
 . The tour begins outside the Weston Branch of the Toronto Public Library 
 at Weston Road and 2 King Street\, and returns to the starting location at
  the end of the walk. TTC bus routes are adjacent.\n\nThis special yearly 
 tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Ple
 ase e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! Yo
 u can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail
 .com**
